-- Layer: not core: lib/bootstrap/match.cub's untyped helpers given types as trusted primitives; they leave the trusted base when match.cub is written with types (the four layers: see the language-implementation-remainder node of task-graph/hyperactivity.cub).
-- lib/bootstrap/exposed.cub — the traversal of codes and rewriting by rules (lib/bootstrap/match.cub), which
-- has no types, given types here as primitives, so that checked code (lib/capacities/specialize.cub,
-- lib/capacities/x86.cub) can use them. Their types are trusted, not checked against the helpers.
-- Loaded after lib/library/std.cub (Rule is checked there).

-- the traversal of codes (lib/bootstrap/match.cub cmap): f p d replaces a part p under d binders, or leaves
-- it to be traversed; shifting free variables up and down
primitive code-map : (Code → Word → Opt Code) → Word → Code → Code = λ f d c → cmap f d c
primitive code-shift : Word → Word → Code → Code = λ d k c → shift-code d k c
primitive code-unshift : Word → Word → Code → Code = λ d b c → unshift-at d b c
-- rewriting (lib/bootstrap/match.cub): a rule's first application in a code, with its path's code; the rules
-- split into those that shrink the code (run to a fixpoint) and the rest
primitive rule-rewrite : Rule → Code → Opt (Code × Code) = λ r c → rewrite-first-path r c
primitive rules-orient : Lst Rule → Lst Rule × Lst Rule = λ rs → orient-rules rs
